Overview

Introduces the 100 Days of Machine Learning series, designed to take learners from beginner to intermediate level through practical, industry-focused training.

Key Points
Covers the complete Machine Learning lifecycle.
Focuses on practical implementation, not just algorithms.
Includes data preprocessing, model selection, training, and deployment.
Machine Learning

Machine Learning enables computers to learn patterns from data and make predictions without being explicitly programmed for every task.

Importance
Widely used in applications like image classification and spam detection.
Driven by the growth of data and computing power.
High demand for Machine Learning professionals.
Conclusion

The series provides a structured learning path that helps learners develop practical Machine Learning skills and become industry-ready.
